Morning. Calm. Wreckage of lanterns and bunting. MORDECAI sits on the step with his report. ROSALIND brings two mugs. TOBIAS enters, soaked, carrying a single enormous crab.

TOBIAS
Morning.

ROSALIND
Tobias!

TOBIAS
I found the sea. It found me back. I followed the light the whole way in. Lost the boat at the harbour mouth, swam the last bit.

ROSALIND
You swam the harbour mouth?

TOBIAS
(holding up the crab)
He helped.

MORDECAI takes out the report. He reads it. He tears out the middle.

MORDECAI
The cost per ship guided, per year, is very high. The cost per ship not guided is higher. I am recommending the light be kept.

ROSALIND
The Admiral won’t like it.

MORDECAI
The Admiral will stamp it. He stamps everything. That is what Fridays are for.

TOBIAS
Will you stay for the festival? I’ve fixed the sign.

He reveals it. It reads ROTCEPSNI. Nobody corrects him.

HETTIE
(off, singing)
~ Lanterns on the water,
~ Lanterns on the hill—

MORDECAI
(to ROSALIND)
The ninth step. Shall I mend it before I go?

ROSALIND
Leave it. It’s how we know who’s counting.

The beam turns once over the audience, in daylight.

> BLACKOUT.
